<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZSE says chairman David Wale to retire next month.</title>
<headline>NZSE says chairman David Wale to retire next month.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The chairman of the New Zealand Stock Exchange, David Wale, will step down next month, managing director Bill Foster tole Reuters on Thursday.</p>
<p>Foster confirmed a report on Radio New Zealand, and said that the exchange would confirm details of Wale's retirement and successor at its annual general meeting scheduled for August 23.</p>
<p>--Wellington newsroom, 64 4 4734 746</p>
<p>e-mail wellington.newsroom@reuters.com</p>
